 To apply a Gaussian filter before the Sobel edge detection in MATLAB, you can use the `imgaussfilt` function to smooth the image and then apply the Sobel operator. Here's the modified code:
```
% Read input image
input_image = imread('image.jpg');
% Convert to grayscale
gray_image = rgb2gray(input_image);
% Define Sobel operators in x and y directions
sobel_x = [-1 0 1; -2 0 2; -1 0 1];
sobel_y = [-1 -2 -1; 0 0 0; 1 2 1];
% Apply Gaussian filter (standard deviation is a parameter, adjust as needed)
gaussian_filter = imgaussfilt(double(gray_image), 2.5);
% Apply Sobel operator in x direction to the filtered image
edge_image_x = conv2(double(gaussian_filter), sobel_x, 'same');
% Apply Sobel operator in y direction to the filtered image
edge_image_y = conv2(double(gaussian_filter), sobel_y, 'same');
% Combine edges in both directions
edge_image = sqrt(edge_image_x.^2 + edge_image_y.^2);
% Display edge image
imshow(edge_image);
```
Adjust the value of the standard deviation in the `imgaussfilt` function according to your specific requirements to control the amount of smoothing applied to the image.

